  "review": [
    "The hymn is a prayer for revival: 1:1–8 is Ps 65:10 with Gal 5:22 and Mal 3:10, the chorus is Ps 80:4 with Ps 80:19 and 2 Chr 7:14, 2:1–8 is John 8:32 with Eph 5:26, and 3:1–8 is Eph 3:17 with Mark 9:24.",
    "The chorus is four lines (the print's [القرار]), placed between stanza 1 and 2; the payload keeps it as the labelled stanza and its three imperative petitions in sequence.",
    "3:8 וְהִתְיַחֵס לְאִטִּיּוּת אֱמוּנָתֵנוּ — the Arabic واتعامل مع بطء إيماننا is 'deal with the slowness of our faith'; the Hebrew uses יִחֵס (post-biblical 'to relate to') with אִטִּיּוּת, because the line asks God to be patient with slowness and must not sound like a rebuke of it."
  ]
